Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id)'s cart is EMPTY at the start (live-discover a served org confirmed to have an empty cart if @td(ORG_ACME.id) does not). Regression target: VCST-5588 found that switching the storefront header currency after filling a cart in currency A DOUBLED the reported item count (the switch copies cart lines into a new-currency cart instead of moving them, and the pre-fix resolver summed quantities across BOTH currencies). Confirmed fixed by scoping the resolver to `currencyCode`.

Assertions:
[STATE] the customer-profile figure after the currency switch (step 9) equals the pre-switch figure (step 6) — switching the DISPLAY currency alone must not change the counted quantity {SPEC}
[STATE] the dashboard roll-up figure (step 11) is consistent with the customer-profile figure for the same organization under the same currency — the two surfaces share one calculation source per the VCST-5587/5588 shared-builder requirement {SPEC}
[STATE] the figure does NOT double after the currency switch — a doubled value reproduces the VCST-5588 pre-fix defect (cart lines copied into the new-currency cart, then summed across both currencies) {SPEC}

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[API] salesRepCustomerCartStatistics for @td(ORG_ACME.id) scoped to currency B returns the SAME selectedItemQuantity as the pre-switch currency-A query, errors[] empty {SPEC}
[API] the customer-profile query and the dashboard roll-up query for the same organization/currency share byte-identical query text and variables except `organizationId`, per the confirmed VCST-5587 shared-builder pattern {SPEC}
[NETWORK] no 4xx/5xx across the currency switch or either page load

